The bug occurs because the driver is unregistered after attempting to remove multi-instance hotplug callbacks. This incorrect order means that the system still expects the driver to be active while it is being removed, leading to warnings from the `__cpuhp_remove_state_cpuslocked` function when the number of remaining instances is not zero.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
unregister_virtio_driver(&virtio_net_driver);
cpuhp_remove_multi_state(CPUHP_VIRT_NET_DEAD);
cpuhp_remove_multi_state(virtionet_online);
```
Reason:
The fix changes the order of operations by unregistering the driver before removing the multi-instance hotplug callbacks. This ensures that the driver is no longer active when the callbacks are being removed, preventing the warnings from occurring when the number of remaining instances is not zero.

